sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User Requesting Reset
    participant Browser as Web Browser
    participant Gateway as API Gateway / Rate Limiter
    participant AuthService as Identity & Auth Service
    participant Database as PostgreSQL Database
    participant MailService as Transactional Email Service
    participant Redis as Redis Session Cache

    Note over User,MailService: Phase 1: Password Reset Request (Generic Anti-Enumeration)
    User->>Browser: Enters email on /forgot-password
    Browser->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password { email }
    Gateway->>Gateway: Check rate limits (3 / 15min per email; 10 / hr per IP)
    Gateway->>AuthService: Forward request
    
    AuthService->>Database: SELECT id, status FROM users WHERE email = :email
    alt Account Exists & Active
        AuthService->>AuthService: Generate 256-bit CSPRNG reset token
        AuthService->>Database: INSERT into password_reset_tokens (token_hash, expires_at=NOW()+15m)
        AuthService->>MailService: Dispatch reset link to unverified contact address
        MailService-->>User: Delivers email with link: https://app.vrm.com/reset-password?token=...
    else Account Does Not Exist
        AuthService->>AuthService: Execute dummy delay to equalize response timing
    end
    
    AuthService-->>Gateway: HTTP 200 OK ("If email matches an account, link dispatched")
    Gateway-->>Browser: HTTP 200 OK
    Browser-->>User: Display generic confirmation message

    Note over User,Redis: Phase 2: Password Reset Execution
    User->>Browser: Clicks reset link in email, enters new password (min 15 chars)
    Browser->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password { token, newPassword }
    Gateway->>AuthService: Forward payload
    
    AuthService->>AuthService: Compute SHA256(token)
    AuthService->>Database: SELECT * FROM password_reset_tokens WHERE token_hash = :hash
    alt Token Invalid, Expired (> 15m), or Already Used (used_at IS NOT NULL)
        AuthService-->>Gateway: HTTP 400 Bad Request ("Token expired or already used")
        Gateway-->>Browser: HTTP 400 Bad Request
        Browser-->>User: Display error; offer new reset request
    else Token Valid & Unused
        AuthService->>AuthService: Hash new password via Argon2id
        AuthService->>Database: UPDATE users SET password_hash = :newHash WHERE id = :userId
        AuthService->>Database: UPDATE password_reset_tokens SET used_at = NOW() WHERE id = :tokenId
        
        Note over AuthService,Redis: Revoke ALL existing active sessions
        AuthService->>Database: UPDATE sessions SET revoked_at = NOW() WHERE user_id = :userId
        AuthService->>Redis: Flush session keys for user_id
        
        AuthService-->>Gateway: HTTP 200 OK ("Password updated successfully")
        Gateway-->>Browser: HTTP 200 OK
        Browser-->>User: Redirect to login view with success notification
    end
